            <listPerson>
                <person xml:id="FIR01" sex="1">
                    <persName>
                        <roleName/>
                        <forename>William</forename>
                        <surname>Firth</surname>
                        <addName/>
                    </persName>
                    <birth when="1000">
                        <placeName> </placeName>
                    </birth>
                    <death when="1000"/>
                    <occupation/>
                    <note type="editorial">William Firth was a member 
    of the Norwich Revolution Society. Godwin's first two meetings with him are at the <persName key="ALD02 ALD04"/>Alderson's, during
  his 1794 visit to Norwich and the next year Firth appears in London at <persName key="HOL01">Thomas Holcroft's</persName>, again in the
  company of <persName key="ALD02">Amelia Alderson</persName>. Over the next few years, when Godwin sees Firth in London it is almost
  always in conjunction with other Norwich contacts (<persName key="TAY03">William Taylor</persName>, <persName key="PLU01 PLU02">the Plumptres</persName>, 
   and <persName key="MAR05">Charles Marsh</persName>), 
which further supports this identification.
  
  </note>
                    <bibl type="printedbook">C.B. Jewson, <title>The Jacobin City: A Portrait of Norwich in its Reaction to the French Revolution 1788-1802</title> (Glasgow: Blackie, 1975)</bibl>
                </person>
            </listPerson>
